@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.854 = private unnamed_addr constant [598 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `pytest.fail` calls without a message.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`pytest.fail` calls without a message make it harder to understand and debug test failures.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Adef test_foo():\0A    pytest.fail()\0A\0A\0Adef test_bar():\0A    pytest.fail(\22\22)\0A\0A\0Adef test_baz():\0A    pytest.fail(reason=\22\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Adef test_foo():\0A    pytest.fail(\22...\22)\0A\0A\0Adef test_bar():\0A    pytest.fail(reason=\22...\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: `pytest.fail`](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/reference.html#pytest-fail)\0A", align 1
